WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:12.150 --> 00:00:17.720
House of the Dragon, a Game of Thrones prequel
show, is coming in 2022 on HBO and beside

00:00:17.720 --> 00:00:22.360
Targaryens themselves, Targaryen dragons will
also play a major role in this upcoming epic

00:00:22.360 --> 00:00:23.430
series.

00:00:23.430 --> 00:00:27.360
Game of Thrones had only 3 dragons and it
was a game changer.

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:32.780
House of the Dragon will feature over 20 dragons
and even more epic dragon fights.

00:00:32.780 --> 00:00:36.460
Dragons are the reason that the dragonlord
Targaryen family frequently married brother

00:00:36.460 --> 00:00:38.850
to sister
to keep the bloodline pure

00:00:38.850 --> 00:00:43.780
as it is generally believed that Valyrian
heritage plays a part in bonding with a dragon.

00:00:43.780 --> 00:00:47.870
Provided it has food and freedom, a dragon
never stops growing.

00:00:47.870 --> 00:00:52.830
The lifespan of dragons is many times that
of a human, although their maximum natural

00:00:52.830 --> 00:00:57.830
lifespan is difficult to determine: as beasts
of war, most of the known examples died in

00:00:57.830 --> 00:00:58.830
battle.

00:00:58.830 --> 00:01:03.140
Balerion, the largest and oldest Targaryen
dragon, already alive when House Targaryen

00:01:03.140 --> 00:01:10.350
relocated from Valyria to Dragonstone in 114
BC died of old age in 94 AC.

00:01:10.350 --> 00:01:14.441
Balerion was near two hundred years of age
when he died, but as the only known example

00:01:14.441 --> 00:01:19.410
of a dragon who died of old age, it is unclear
if this should be considered typical.

00:01:19.410 --> 00:01:22.190
The Valyrians had thousands of dragons.

00:01:22.190 --> 00:01:27.830
After the Doom of Valyria, however, the only
dragons known to have survived were five dragons

00:01:27.830 --> 00:01:29.180
on Dragonstone.

00:01:29.180 --> 00:01:33.790
They belonged to House Targaryen, who had
brought them from Valyria when they went into

00:01:33.790 --> 00:01:34.790
exile.

00:01:34.790 --> 00:01:39.040
Four of these dragons eventually died on Dragonstone,
leaving only Balerion.

00:01:39.040 --> 00:01:44.810
However, the other dragons left eggs behind,
and from these hatched Vhagar and Meraxes.

00:01:44.810 --> 00:01:51.620
Balerion, called the Black Dread, was ridden
by King Aegon I Targaryen during his Conquest.

00:01:51.620 --> 00:01:55.110
Balerion was the largest and oldest Targaryen
dragon ever.

00:01:55.110 --> 00:02:00.990
His wingspan was so large that his shadow
could engulf entire towns when he passed overhead.

00:02:00.990 --> 00:02:06.630
His teeth were as long as swords, and his
jaws were large enough to swallow a mammoth.

00:02:06.630 --> 00:02:11.370
Beside by Aegon the Conqueror, Balerion was
also ridden by Maegor the Cruel, Princess

00:02:11.370 --> 00:02:15.510
Aerea Targaryen and King Viserys I Targaryen.

00:02:15.510 --> 00:02:17.489
Balerion's scales and wings were black.

00:02:17.489 --> 00:02:19.349
His fire was black as well.

00:02:19.349 --> 00:02:24.099
When he was in the fullness of his power,
his flames could melt steel and stone, and

00:02:24.099 --> 00:02:25.989
fuse sand into glass.

00:02:25.989 --> 00:02:30.310
House Targaryen used Balerion, Vhagar, and
Meraxes in their Wars of Conquest against

00:02:30.310 --> 00:02:31.420
the Seven Kingdoms.

00:02:31.420 --> 00:02:36.750
They were instrumental in the burning of Harrenhal
and the Field of Fire, and the threat of dragons

00:02:36.750 --> 00:02:40.599
led to the submissions of Torrhen Stark and
Sharra Arryn.

00:02:40.599 --> 00:02:44.689
Dragons were also used in the First Dornish
War, which caused the death of Meraxes at

00:02:44.689 --> 00:02:46.999
the Hellholt in 10 AC.

00:02:46.999 --> 00:02:52.819
She was ridden by Queen Rhaenys Targaryen
and was named for one of the gods of Old Valyria.

00:02:52.819 --> 00:02:57.040
Meraxes was larger than Vhagar, but smaller
than Balerion.

00:02:57.040 --> 00:02:59.019
She could swallow horses whole.

00:02:59.019 --> 00:03:01.920
Meraxes had golden eyes and silver scales.

00:03:01.920 --> 00:03:07.290
While being ridden by Queen Rhaenys in their
invasion of Dorne, an iron bolt from a scorpion

00:03:07.290 --> 00:03:12.529
went through Meraxes's eye, and the dragon
and Rhaenys fell from the sky to their deaths.

00:03:12.529 --> 00:03:15.620
Many dragons were hatched after Aegon's Conquest.

00:03:15.620 --> 00:03:20.420
During Aegon I's reign, "half a dozen" hatchlings
were born on Dragonstone.

00:03:20.420 --> 00:03:26.230
One of the first was Quicksilver, hatched
in 7 AC, who bonded with Aegon I's elder son

00:03:26.230 --> 00:03:27.890
and heir, Aenys.

00:03:27.890 --> 00:03:32.709
Quarter the size of Balerion, her fireballs
were pale white in color.

00:03:32.709 --> 00:03:37.480
Quicksilver died in 43 AC in what became the
first time since the Doom of Valyria that

00:03:37.480 --> 00:03:39.419
a dragon fought dragon.

00:03:39.419 --> 00:03:44.609
In the battle Beneath the Gods Eye, Aegon
the Conqueror's grandson, also named Aegon,

00:03:44.609 --> 00:03:49.870
attempted to win back the throne that by rights
was his, but both Quicksilver and Aegon died

00:03:49.870 --> 00:03:53.420
fighting Maegor upon his dragon Balerion.

00:03:53.420 --> 00:03:57.900
Balerion grabbed Quicksilver's throat in his
jaws, then ripped one of Quicksilver's wings

00:03:57.900 --> 00:04:04.189
from its body in mid-air, after which Quicksilver
fell to its death, along with young Aegon.

00:04:04.189 --> 00:04:09.049
Over the course of one hundred and fifty years
the Targaryens rode their dragons as a symbol

00:04:09.049 --> 00:04:10.730
of their power.

00:04:10.730 --> 00:04:15.609
King Jaehaerys I Targaryen took six dragons
with him to Winterfell to visit the Warden

00:04:15.609 --> 00:04:16.910
of the North.

00:04:16.910 --> 00:04:23.300
These included Jaehaerys on Vermithor, Queen
Alysanne on Silverwing, and four other currently-unknown

00:04:23.300 --> 00:04:24.300
dragons.

00:04:24.300 --> 00:04:28.650
Vermithor, called the Bronze Fury, was a male
dragon.

00:04:28.650 --> 00:04:31.830
Vermithor was already a large dragon in 48
AC.

00:04:31.830 --> 00:04:34.069
Only larger were Balerion and Vhagar.

00:04:34.069 --> 00:04:39.240
By the time of the Dance of the Dragons, Vermithor
was almost a hundred years old.

00:04:39.240 --> 00:04:45.560
Balerion finally died of old age in 94 AC,
late in the reign of Jaehaerys I. Jaehaerys's

00:04:45.560 --> 00:04:51.949
grandson and eventual successor Viserys I
was Balerion's rider at the time of its death.

00:04:51.949 --> 00:04:58.360
This left Vhagar as the largest living dragon,
and by 129 AC she was approaching Balerion's

00:04:58.360 --> 00:04:59.360
size.

00:04:59.360 --> 00:05:03.960
By the end of the reign of King Viserys I
Targaryen, twenty dragons were alive.

00:05:03.960 --> 00:05:08.229
The majority of these died during the civil
war called the Dance of the Dragons, which

00:05:08.229 --> 00:05:13.389
began in 129 AC and lasted until mid 131 AC.

00:05:13.389 --> 00:05:17.509
The Dance of the Dragons was the most devastating
war in the history of the Seven Kingdoms.

00:05:17.509 --> 00:05:22.840
A war of succession between Aegon II and his
half-sister Rhaenyra over their father Viserys

00:05:22.840 --> 00:05:24.379
I's throne.

00:05:24.379 --> 00:05:26.740
Both of them thought they belonged on the
Iron Throne.

00:05:26.740 --> 00:05:31.389
When people started declaring for one of them
or the other, their fight divided the kingdoms

00:05:31.389 --> 00:05:32.539
in two.

00:05:32.539 --> 00:05:37.360
Targaryens fought Targaryens, bothers fought
brothers, dragons fought dragons.

00:05:37.360 --> 00:05:39.800
By the time it was over, thousands were dead.

00:05:39.800 --> 00:05:44.030
The conflict would prove to be incredibly
destructive for not only House Targaryen,

00:05:44.030 --> 00:05:46.099
but large parts of Westeros as well.

00:05:46.099 --> 00:05:50.949
In addition, it devastated the Targaryen's
dragon population, ultimately leading to their

00:05:50.949 --> 00:05:52.720
extinction within a few decades.

00:05:52.720 --> 00:05:54.960
They never truly recovered.

00:05:54.960 --> 00:06:00.189
The largest and oldest dragons during the
Targaryen civil war were Vhagar, Vermithor,

00:06:00.189 --> 00:06:03.669
Silverwing, Dreamfyre, Meleys, Caraxes, and
Syrax.

00:06:03.669 --> 00:06:08.689
The younger dragons still large enough to
be ridden to war were Seasmoke, Sunfyre, Tessarion,

00:06:08.689 --> 00:06:11.939
Vermax, Arrax, Tyraxes, and Moondancer.

00:06:11.939 --> 00:06:16.569
Stormcloud, Morghul, and Shrykos were hatchlings
not yet big enough to ride.

00:06:16.569 --> 00:06:21.900
There were also three wild dragons living
on Dragonstone which had never been successfully

00:06:21.900 --> 00:06:26.750
claimed by any rider: Grey Ghost, Sheepstealer,
and the Cannibal.

00:06:26.750 --> 00:06:29.460
Syrax was Rhaenyra Targaryen's dragon.

00:06:29.460 --> 00:06:32.430
Her name came from a goddess of Valyria.

00:06:32.430 --> 00:06:34.490
Syrax had yellow scales.

00:06:34.490 --> 00:06:40.189
She was huge and formidable, but not as fearsome
or experienced in battle as Daemon's Caraxes.

00:06:40.189 --> 00:06:43.419
She was kept in chains and exceedingly well
fed.

00:06:43.419 --> 00:06:47.210
Syrax was slain in the aftermath of the Storming
of the Dragonpit.

00:06:47.210 --> 00:06:51.720
Prince Joffrey had attempted to mount her
to ride to the Dragonpit, save the other dragons,

00:06:51.720 --> 00:06:55.050
and perhaps mount his own dragon Tyraxes there.

00:06:55.050 --> 00:07:00.350
However, dragons are not horses, and they
will only accept one mount at a time.

00:07:00.350 --> 00:07:04.819
In mid-flight, Syrax shrugged off Joffrey,
who fell to his death.

00:07:04.819 --> 00:07:08.330
Syrax eventually died fighting the rioters
on the ground.

00:07:08.330 --> 00:07:14.150
In 129 AC, after the start of the Dance of
the Dragons, the second biggest dragon alive,

00:07:14.150 --> 00:07:18.550
Vermithor bent his neck to a blacksmith’s
bastard called Hugh Hammer.

00:07:18.550 --> 00:07:23.449
During the Second Battle of Tumbleton
Addam Velaryon upon the dragon Seasmoke attacked

00:07:23.449 --> 00:07:24.449
Vermithor.

00:07:24.449 --> 00:07:27.219
Seasmoke was a pale silver-grey dragon.

00:07:27.219 --> 00:07:31.620
It was of fighting size during the Dance,
but still a young dragon and nimbler in the

00:07:31.620 --> 00:07:33.249
air than his older brothers.

00:07:33.249 --> 00:07:38.749
He was of comparable size to Tessarion, who
was about three times smaller than Vermithor,

00:07:38.749 --> 00:07:42.000
and not as fearsome a beast as him in comparison.

00:07:42.000 --> 00:07:45.810
Just before this, Vermithor's rider was killed.

00:07:45.810 --> 00:07:51.910
Vermithor, now riderless, wounded and enraged,
took flight, attacking all those around him.

00:07:51.910 --> 00:07:56.430
While Vermithor was only twenty feet above
the field, Seasmoke slammed into him from

00:07:56.430 --> 00:07:57.430
above.

00:07:57.430 --> 00:08:02.659
The two dragons rolled over the field, so
entangled that neither was able to break free.

00:08:02.659 --> 00:08:04.939
Tessarion also entered the fight.

00:08:04.939 --> 00:08:07.110
The three dragons fought to the death.

00:08:07.110 --> 00:08:10.810
Tessarion, also known as the Blue Queen, was
a she-dragon.

00:08:10.810 --> 00:08:13.289
She was ridden by Prince Daeron Targaryen.

00:08:13.289 --> 00:08:18.719
Tessarion was a beautiful blue she-dragon
and her flames were cobalt blue in color.

00:08:18.719 --> 00:08:21.770
She was one of the smaller fighting dragons.

00:08:21.770 --> 00:08:26.360
Vermithor killed Seasmoke when he locked his
teeth into the latter's neck and ripped his

00:08:26.360 --> 00:08:27.360
head off.

00:08:27.360 --> 00:08:33.150
He attempted to take flight with his prize
still in his jaws, but his wings were tattered,

00:08:33.150 --> 00:08:35.820
causing him to be unable to bear the weight.

00:08:35.820 --> 00:08:38.000
After a moment he collapsed and died.

00:08:38.000 --> 00:08:40.020
Tessarion was the last to die.

00:08:40.020 --> 00:08:44.950
On three occasions did she try to fly again,
but failed every time again.

00:08:44.950 --> 00:08:48.890
By late afternoon the day after the battle,
she seemed to be in pain.

00:08:48.890 --> 00:08:53.830
At the command of Lord Benjicot Blackwood,
his best archer shot three arrows into the

00:08:53.830 --> 00:08:56.080
dying dragon's eye, killing her.

00:08:56.080 --> 00:09:01.660
The fourth dragon, Silverwing was also there,
but fled into the sky when the battle began.

00:09:01.660 --> 00:09:07.250
However after the battle was over, Silverwing
descended to land beside the slain dragons.

00:09:07.250 --> 00:09:12.080
Later, the singers would tell of how she tried
to lift dead Vermithor’s wing three times

00:09:12.080 --> 00:09:16.330
with her nose, as if to try and make him fly
again.

00:09:16.330 --> 00:09:18.810
Silverwing was a silvery she-dragon.

00:09:18.810 --> 00:09:24.660
She was ridden by Queen Alysanne Targaryen,
and by Ulf White during the Dance of the Dragons.

00:09:24.660 --> 00:09:29.660
Silverwing was the one of only four dragons
still alive at the end of the Targaryen civil

00:09:29.660 --> 00:09:30.770
war.

00:09:30.770 --> 00:09:35.130
During this time of the Dance of the Dragons,
Vhagar was the hardened survivor of a hundred

00:09:35.130 --> 00:09:40.700
battles, had grown almost as large as Balerion,
and was the oldest and largest of the dragons

00:09:40.700 --> 00:09:41.790
in Westeros.

00:09:41.790 --> 00:09:47.070
Her roar was so powerful that it could shake
the very foundations of Storm's End.

00:09:47.070 --> 00:09:50.690
No living dragon could match her for size
or ferocity.

00:09:50.690 --> 00:09:56.380
The color of Vhagar's scales, horns, wings,
wing bones, and spinal crest is unknown, as

00:09:56.380 --> 00:09:58.430
is the color of her flame.

00:09:58.430 --> 00:10:00.710
Prince Aemond was her dragonrider.

00:10:00.710 --> 00:10:05.870
At the beginning of the war, Vhagar killed
young dragon Arrax along with its dragonrider

00:10:05.870 --> 00:10:06.920
Lucerys.

00:10:06.920 --> 00:10:09.450
Arrax was five times smaller than Vhagar.

00:10:09.450 --> 00:10:14.350
The storming of the Dragonpit took place during
the riot of King's Landing during the Dance

00:10:14.350 --> 00:10:20.700
of the Dragons when the rioters slew 4 dragons:
Shrykos, young dragon unclaimed since the

00:10:20.700 --> 00:10:26.690
death of Prince Jaehaerys Targaryen; Morghul,
the dragon of Princess Jaehaera Targaryen;

00:10:26.690 --> 00:10:32.870
Tyraxes, the dragon ridden by Prince Joffrey
Velaryon; and pale blue dragon, Dreamfyre,

00:10:32.870 --> 00:10:36.310
unclaimed since Queen Helaena Targaryen's
death.

00:10:36.310 --> 00:10:40.850
Unable to fly away, as they had been chained,
the four dragons fought with their horns,

00:10:40.850 --> 00:10:42.290
claws, and teeth.

00:10:42.290 --> 00:10:47.460
They let loose their dragonflame and transformed
the Dragonpit into a fiery inferno.

00:10:47.460 --> 00:10:52.880
The first dragon to die was Shrykos, who was
slain by Hobb who leaped onto her neck and

00:10:52.880 --> 00:10:56.080
drove his axe down into the dragon's skull.

00:10:56.080 --> 00:11:01.430
Next died Morghul, slain by the Burning Knight,
who rushed into the dragon's flame and stabbed

00:11:01.430 --> 00:11:05.500
him repeatedly in the eye with his spear as
he burned to his own death.

00:11:05.500 --> 00:11:10.300
Tyraxes burned those who rushed at him from
his lair, until the front entrance of his

00:11:10.300 --> 00:11:12.730
lair was completely blocked with corpses.

00:11:12.730 --> 00:11:17.760
However, the mob broke through the back door
of the dragon's lair and slew him.

00:11:17.760 --> 00:11:19.670
Last to die was Dreamfyre.

00:11:19.670 --> 00:11:24.970
Dreamfyre was the only dragon able to break
free of her chains when the mob broke in.

00:11:24.970 --> 00:11:31.300
She took wing, circled the interior of the
dome and swooped down to attack the men below.

00:11:31.300 --> 00:11:34.890
She slew more men than the other three dragons
combined.

00:11:34.890 --> 00:11:40.040
Archers and crossbowmen loosed arrows and
quarrels at her, and whenever she landed men

00:11:40.040 --> 00:11:44.440
swarmed her to attack, driving her back into
the air.

00:11:44.440 --> 00:11:47.760
Eventually one of her eyes was nicked by a
crossbow bolt.

00:11:47.760 --> 00:11:53.480
Half-blind and maddened, Dreamfyre flew into
the Dragonpit's great dome above, which cracked

00:11:53.480 --> 00:11:54.780
on impact.

00:11:54.780 --> 00:11:58.180
Half of it came tumbling down crushing her
and the dragonslayers

00:11:58.180 --> 00:12:00.990
under tons of broken stone and rubble.

00:12:00.990 --> 00:12:06.030
So many dragons had died in the war that the
Targaryens couldn't maintain a stable breeding

00:12:06.030 --> 00:12:09.910
population, and the few survivors became inbred
and sickly.

00:12:09.910 --> 00:12:14.410
Fortunatlely, however, the key event of House
of the Dragon is the exact same event which

00:12:14.410 --> 00:12:19.710
led to their extinction - the Targaryen civil
war, the Dance of the Dragons and we'll get

00:12:19.710 --> 00:12:21.280
to see them all on screen.

00:12:21.280 --> 00:12:26.410
Part 2 of this video is coming tomorrow when
I will cover even more dragons, in fact some

00:12:26.410 --> 00:12:28.570
of the most epic dragons and their fights.

00:12:28.570 --> 00:12:33.780
A lot of dragons, a lot of epic dragon battles,
all of that and more this Game of Thrones

00:12:33.780 --> 00:12:38.300
prequel series, House of the Dragons brings
in 2022 on HBO.

00:12:38.300 --> 00:12:42.050
Let me know your thoughts about everything:
the prequel, the mighty dragons and their

00:12:42.050 --> 00:12:44.510
epic battles in the comment section down below.

00:12:44.510 --> 00:12:47.570
Thank you so much for watching, hope you enjoyed
this video and if you did make sure to give

00:12:47.570 --> 00:12:55.540
it a big thumbs upand I hope to see you in
the next one, peace!

